title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Agathe: Out of my kitchen! Oh. The map maker. Sit, then, if you must.
Agathe: The Countess wants a feast tonight for the abbey's men, and I have no ale and no flour. The village has both.
Agathe: Hedda's ale and Bram's flour. Bring me those, and you'll eat at the high table.
-> I will go down to the village for you.
    Agathe: Quick, then. The road is an hour each way.
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Active>>
-> I have work here.
    Agathe: Everybody has work here. Nobody has flour.
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed feast>>
===

title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Offered
---
Agathe: Well? Ale and flour?
-> I will fetch them.
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed feast>>
    Agathe: Quick, then.
-> Not yet.
===

title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active
---
<<if has_item("ale") and has_item("flour")>>
    Agathe: Ale! Flour! You beautiful creature.
    <<take ale>>
    <<take flour>>
    <<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
        Agathe: And Hedda sent her mother's fair cake? She's never let that recipe out of the inn. You must have charmed her.
    <<endif>>
    <<set $feast_served to true>>
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed feast>>
<<else>>
    <<if has_item("ale")>>
        Agathe: Still no flour? The abbey's men will eat the tablecloth.
    <<elseif has_item("flour")>>
        Agathe: Still no ale? The abbey's men will drink the well.
    <<else>>
        Agathe: Nothing yet? Hedda's ale and Bram's flour. It isn't hard.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Agathe
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
when: $quest_feast != QuestState.NotStarted and $quest_feast != QuestState.Offered and $quest_feast != QuestState.Active
---
=> Agathe: Everything in this castle is cold except my kitchen.
=> Agathe: Corvin eats standing up. Never trust a man who eats standing up.
=> Agathe: The feast was a triumph. The abbot's men cried into the soup. <<if $feast_served>>
===

title: Events
act: Castle
location: Village
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: once
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: here() == "Village" and been_to("Castle")
---
// The village after a day away: what changed while the cartographer was at the castle. Not before the castle: the
// summons sets the act in the village, and the journey waits for the end of the dialogue and of its events.
The village looks smaller after the castle.
Pell's cart is gone from the green. He went up the hill to sell to the castle.
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    The boundary stones stand where the sergeant left them. Nobody moved them last night.
<<else>>
    The boundary stones have moved again. One more pace up the bank.
<<endif>>
===

title: Hedda
act: Castle
location: Inn
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active and not has_item("ale")
---
Hedda: Ale for the castle? Agathe sent you? She'd send the river if it could carry a cask.
<<give ale>>
<<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Hedda: And take this cake for the high table. My mother's recipe. Tell Agathe whose it is.
<<endif>>
===

title: Hedda
act: All
location: Inn
scenario: The feast
when: always
---
=> Hedda: Soup's on. It's always on.
=> Hedda: The regulars are Wim and Saul. They have argued about the same cow for nine years. <<if $act == Act.Survey>>
=> Hedda: Corvin drinks here when the castle is too quiet for him. He pays, I'll give him that. <<if $act == Act.Survey>>
=> Hedda: Lio was out late again. I saw the lantern go down to the river. <<if $act == Act.Survey and not $saw_lio>>
=> Hedda: Bram will lose the mill if the road goes straight. He won't say it, but he's afraid. <<if $act == Act.Survey>>
=> Hedda: The castle has you running errands? That's a castle for you. <<if $act == Act.Castle>>
=> Hedda: The cake is in the oven for the fair. <<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
=> Hedda: The regulars talk of nothing but Jory. <<if $act == Act.Fair>>
===

title: Bram
act: Castle
location: Village
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active and not has_item("flour")
---
<<if $wheel_mended>>
    Bram: Flour for the castle's feast? The wheel ground all night. Take a sack, and tell the Countess it's Oster flour.
    <<give flour>>
<<else>>
    Bram: Flour? With the wheel stuck? I have none to give, not even to a Countess. #mood:sad
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitFounder
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitFounder") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    The founder of the house of Varne, in gold armour, with a map unrolled at his feet. The border on it runs under a hill.
<<else>>
    The founder again. He looks at you as if you owe him rent.
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitTwins
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitTwins") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    Two sisters, the same face twice. One of them married an abbot's brother, and the border moved a mile.
<<else>>
    The twins. One of them is smiling. You are not sure it was the same one last time.
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitSaint
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitSaint") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
<<endif>>
// The castle's runner chooses among line groups with its own saliency strategy: the lines come round in order
=> A pale lady in blue, holding a lantern. The plate says "Saint of the Deep Ways".
=> The lantern in the painting is green, like no flame you have ever seen.
=> The lady in blue again. Her lantern lights a carved wall behind her.
===

title: PortraitHound
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitHound") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    A hound. Just a hound. The plate says "Biscuit, who found the well".
<<elseif visited_count("PortraitHound") == 1>>
    Biscuit again. A good dog. A great dog, by the look of the frame.
<<else>>
    You have looked at this dog [plural value={visited_count("PortraitHound") + 1} one="% time" other="% times" /] now.
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitSeen
act: Castle
location: Castle
quest: portraits
---
// Said the first time each portrait is looked at, after it is counted.
<<if $portraits_seen >= 4>>
    <<set $quest_portraits to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed portraits>>
<<elseif $quest_portraits == QuestState.NotStarted>>
    <<set $quest_portraits to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed portraits>>
<<endif>>
===
